    "verdict": "go-with-conditions",
    "headline": "A small app with every classic .NET Framework trap in it. Worth moving incrementally - after two decisions: how sign-in and the session cart work while both apps run.",
    "destination": "Port to .NET 10 incrementally (strangler fig): new ASP.NET Core host with YARP in front, System.Web adapters for shared code, CoreWCF for the inventory service, EF 6.5 as a bridge before EF Core.",
    "verdictReason": "Nothing blocks the move for good: the 4 hard blockers (HttpContext.Current in a library, BinaryFormatter, the WCF server, System.Web in a library) all have known fixes. The risk is behavior, not code - 9 pricing and cart quirks that customers see. Lock them with parity tests before touching anything, then move the read-only pages and the API first."
